as crept up slightly, but only by a few points.\n- **Skew:** It is flat, so the market isn't charging extra for downside or upside protection. That makes it neither a cheap nor an expensive time to buy one side.\n\nPricing alone doesn't make a case for adding to the position. If you do add, the reason should come from your view on the underlying business rather than from the options being cheap.\n\nOne risk to that view is customer concentration. Utilities are 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham Power is 35% of those utility orders and Norvane is 21%. Another node found that data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026. Neither point shows up in the option pricing.\n\nI only had the snapshot and the three yearly volatility points. I did not have the actual premiums, strikes or expiries, so I couldn't compare realized volatility against implied.\n\nSources: the `vltx-leaps` snapshot, the `vltx_iv_history` series, and the `vltx-order-mix` document.","ttft_ms":1786,"type":"result","duration_ms":16956,"uuid":"7a73fff2-9157-4603-8341-5374fc96118f","ttft_stream_ms":1024,"time_to_request_ms":79,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":8,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":14,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":17,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":72,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":187,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":113,"process_rss_mib_result":196,"process_anon_mib_result":115,"process_peak_rss_mib":196,"process_cpu_ms_turn":541,"process_wall_ms_turn":16956,"process_cpu_ms_